0..76 Comment "//! A pair whose first field holds a function, and whose second field\'s type"
77..97 Comment "//! reads the first."
98..101 Comment "//!"
102..175 Comment "//! The type of the second field of `Pair(a, b)` is `b(x)`. When `x` is a"
176..247 Comment "//! function, the type must read the function as some value. A function"
248..324 Comment "//! written as a lambda returns no value, so the type cannot read it as one."
325..328 Comment "//!"
329..403 Comment "//! The type reads the function as the thunk it stands for. The family can"
404..439 Comment "//! read its argument or ignore it."
440..443 Comment "//!"
444..460 Comment "//! - see: #5374"
461..543 Comment "//! - see: #5353 — a lambda argument that a later type reads stands as its thunk"
